cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "geodesic-integrators"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Systematic comparison of explicit Runge-Kutta (RK4, DP5, DOP853), Gauss-Legendre (orders 2,
  4, 6) and Tao (orders 2, 4) integrators for timelike and null geodesics around a
  Schwarzschild black hole, in the second-order and the Hamiltonian formulation, validated
  against closed-form solutions. Covers error growth over 10^4 orbits, conservation of
  invariants, cost per accuracy, and the photon sphere and ISCO. Every figure, table and the
  report are reproduced by one command.
authors:
  - family-names: Saputra
    given-names: Nugie
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NugiePhysics/geodesic-integrators"
url: "https://nugiephysics.github.io/geodesic-integrators/"
keywords:
  - general relativity
  - black hole
  - geodesics
  - Schwarzschild metric
  - symplectic integrators
  - geometric numerical integration
  - Runge-Kutta
